From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:38:21 +0100
Subject: irqchip/mips-gic: Fix local timer/perfctr/fdc on single-cluster
 systems

Commit d1cb1437b785 ("irqchip/mips-gic: Prevent indirect access to
clusters without CPU cores") made gic_mask_local_irq_all_vpes() and
gic_unmask_local_irq_all_vpes() return early when all CPUs are in one
cluster, and it made gic_irq_domain_map() skip the map register write
for local interrupts in that case.

On a single-cluster system, the CP0 timer, performance counter and FDC
interrupts therefore stay masked on every CPU if the GIC routes them.
The boot CPU runs gic_cpu_startup() before any of these interrupts is
mapped, and since gic_irq_domain_map() and
gic_unmask_local_irq_all_vpes() no longer write the map and mask
registers, the interrupts remain unmapped and masked on the boot CPU.
The secondary CPUs keep the interrupts masked because
gic_unmask_local_irq_all_vpes() returns before it sets cd->mask, which
gic_all_vpes_irq_cpu_online() checks when a CPU comes online.

If the CP0 timer is the clock event device, the boot hangs in
calibrate_delay() and the console output stops before the "Calibrating
delay loop..." line.

Drop the three single-cluster checks, so that the driver writes these
registers on every online CPU again. for_each_online_cpu_gic() only
visits online CPUs, and an online CPU is never in a cluster without CPU
cores, so the loop never accesses such a cluster.

Fixes: d1cb1437b785 ("irqchip/mips-gic: Prevent indirect access to clusters without CPU cores")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4-7
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/irq-mips-gic.c b/drivers/irqchip/irq-mips-gic.c
index 19a57c5e2b2e..8e6710857e5c 100644
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-mips-gic.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-mips-gic.c
@@ -512,9 +512,6 @@ static void gic_mask_local_irq_all_vpes(struct irq_data *d)
 	struct gic_all_vpes_chip_data *cd;
 	int intr, cpu;
 
-	if (!mips_cps_multicluster_cpus())
-		return;
-
 	intr = GIC_HWIRQ_TO_LOCAL(d->hwirq);
 	cd = irq_data_get_irq_chip_data(d);
 	cd->mask = false;
@@ -528,9 +525,6 @@ static void gic_unmask_local_irq_all_vpes(struct irq_data *d)
 	struct gic_all_vpes_chip_data *cd;
 	int intr, cpu;
 
-	if (!mips_cps_multicluster_cpus())
-		return;
-
 	intr = GIC_HWIRQ_TO_LOCAL(d->hwirq);
 	cd = irq_data_get_irq_chip_data(d);
 	cd->mask = true;
@@ -698,10 +692,8 @@ static int gic_irq_domain_map(struct irq_domain *d, unsigned int virq,
 	if (!gic_local_irq_is_routable(intr))
 		return -EPERM;
 
-	if (mips_cps_multicluster_cpus()) {
-		for_each_online_cpu_gic(cpu, &gic_lock)
-			write_gic_vo_map(mips_gic_vx_map_reg(intr), map);
-	}
+	for_each_online_cpu_gic(cpu, &gic_lock)
+		write_gic_vo_map(mips_gic_vx_map_reg(intr), map);
 
 	return 0;
 }
